            <ArticleTitle>Antimicrobial stewardship in pediatric post-acute care facilities.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0196-6553(17)31137-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajic.2017.09.031</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Providers in pediatric post-acute care facilities were surveyed about knowledge of and resources for antimicrobial stewardship. All agreed that antibiotics were overused in such pediatric facilities, but 60% had not implemented stewardship strategies. Lack of treatment guidelines (47%) was identified as the most common barrier to antimicrobial stewardship.</AbstractText>
